# Scacelith - Suomi (Finnish)
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: one|other (1 is "one").
# Register: the player is "sinä" (2nd person singular), as Finnish software writes; buttons are
# imperatives ("Tallenna", "Peruuta") or nouns ("Asetukset"); sentence case, titles in capitals.
# Chess words follow the Finnish glossary: valkea / musta (lower case in running text), sotilas,
# ratsu, lähetti, torni, kuningatar, kuningas; letters K D T L R; rated / casual = pisteytetty /
# pisteyttämätön. No case ending is ever put on a {n} placeholder: the sentence inflects a noun
# beside it ("pelaajan {0} lippu", "palvelimelle {0}") or leaves the placeholder in the nominative.
# Counted nouns after a figure: "{0} siirron jälkeen", "{0} siirrolla" (one form fits every number).

